# --- registry -------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by setup/lib/models.sh; passed to llama-server as environment and
# ignored there. MODEL_SWA=yes means the profile MUST carry --swa-full —
# without it every Claude Code turn re-processes the whole prompt.
MODEL_TITLE=Prose · 16.4 GiB · dense · QAT-q4_0 · prose sampling
MODEL_SWA=yes
# MODEL_SOURCE — where this model comes from, so the profile can fetch it.
# `<repo> <pattern>…`: every pattern is a substring of a path in that repo and
# every matching .gguf is fetched, so a sharded quant comes down whole and an
# mmproj rides along. Read by setup/get-model.sh, which is this stack's
# equivalent of `ollama pull` — except that the list it offers is MEASURED on
# this hardware (bash setup/lib/models.sh table) rather than a generic catalog.
# Verified 26.08. by matching the exact filename in the repo, not by guessing.
MODEL_SOURCE=google/gemma-4-31B-it-qat-q4_0-gguf gemma-4-31B_q4_0-it gemma-4-31B-it-mmproj
# MODEL_KV_KIB_PER_TOKEN — what one token of context costs in KV cache,
# MEASURED. Read by setup/lib/budget.py, which refuses a start that would not
# fit before it can freeze the machine. This was the last profile without one.
#
# TWO-POINT, and the second point is what makes it a measurement rather than a
# bound. Two loads under bench/sideserver.py, production stopped, GTT down to
# 0.8 GiB before each:
#
#     -c  32768    GTT 23.07 GiB    23.07 - 17.56 weights = 5.51
#     -c 131072    GTT 27.24 GiB                          = 9.68
#     ---------------------------------------------------------
#     4.17 GiB over 98,304 tokens  ->  44.5 KiB/token, plus 4.12 GiB constant
#
# Weights and compute buffers are constant in -c and cancel in the difference.
# A SINGLE reading cannot do that: it charges the whole constant to the KV and
# reads 176 KiB/token at -c 32768 — four times high. The instruction that used
# to stand here said to take one.
#
# THE SHAPE IS THE ARCHITECTURE, not a curve fit. Gemma 3 alternates 5 sliding
# layers to 1 global; at 60 layers that is 50 whose KV the window caps and 10
# that grow with -c. So 44.5 is the marginal cost of ten layers — 4.45 KiB per
# layer per token — and the constant decomposes as 50 x 1024 x 4.45 = 0.22 GiB
# of capped SWA KV plus 3.90 GiB of compute buffers, which lands inside the
# 3.1-4.6 GiB measured independently across nine bench reports.
#
# IT IS TIED TO THIS PROFILE AS IT STANDS. The figure holds only while
# --swa-full is ABSENT. Adding it — the open item about the three MODEL_SWA
# profiles — makes all 60 layers grow with -c instead of 10, so the per-token
# cost goes up roughly sixfold. Re-measure before adding the switch, do not
# carry this number across it.
#
# AND IT IS TIED TO q8_0 KV, which is what -ctk/-ctv below select. On f16 it
# roughly doubles. Two ties, one number: this is why MODEL_KV_SOURCE has to
# say how a figure was taken and not only when.
MODEL_KV_KIB_PER_TOKEN=44.5
MODEL_KV_SOURCE=27.08.2026, two-point under bench/sideserver.py at -c 32768 and -c 131072 (GTT 23.07 and 27.24 GiB, weights 17.56), so weights and buffers cancel. Valid only WITHOUT --swa-full: 50 of 60 layers are sliding and capped, 10 are global and grow.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prose · 16.4 GiB · dense · QAT-q4_0 · SWA 50/60
# Sampling for prose, NOT the coding defaults (runbook section 7)
# -cram WAS 32768, and the reasoning was gemma26's: the old value was copied
# rather than computed, and on a 64 GB Strix Halo it was the only thing
# keeping this profile from fitting — 69.6 of 62 against 43.6.
#
# 6144 was then chosen against an ESTIMATED KV cost, which is no longer the
# state: with the measured 44.5 KiB/token a full window is 1.39 GiB and 6144
# buys 4.3 of them (python3 setup/lib/budget.py --cache). The line the
# estimate wrote said "~3". It is computed now rather than bounded, which is
# what the sentence that stood here asked for.
LLAMA_ARGS=--alias gemma31 -m @MODELS@/gemma-4-31B_q4_0-it.gguf --mmproj @MODELS@/gemma-4-31B-it-mmproj.gguf \
  -ngl 999 -fa on -ub 512 -b 2048 -c 32768 -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 \
  --kv-unified -cram 6144 -ctxcp 64 -cms 4096 \
  --temp 0.9 --top-p 0.92 --jinja --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8082

# Backend for this profile. Measured 24.08. (docs/MODELS.md): the choice
# is MODEL-dependent — Vulkan wins for models without speculation, ROCm wins
# 2x once MTP/ngram speculation is on. Inert until llama-user@.service is
# switched to: ExecStart=/bin/sh -c 'exec "$HOME/$LLAMA_BIN" $LLAMA_ARGS' (one sudo install).
LLAMA_BIN=llama.cpp/build-vulkan/bin/llama-server
